HOW TO ADD A NEW TEST CLASS
────────────────────────────
1. Create YourTests.java in src/test/java/tests/ extending BaseTest
2. Copy the <test> block template below and fill in your class name
3. Save — Maven will pick it up on the next `mvn test`

TEMPLATE:
    <test name="Your Feature Tests">
        <classes>
            <class name="tests.YourTests"/>
        </classes>
    </test>

HOW TO SKIP A TEST CLASS TEMPORARILY
──────────────────────────────────────
Wrap the <test> block in a comment:
    <!-
    <test name="Cart Tests">
        <classes>
            <class name="tests.CartTests"/>
        </classes>
    </test>
    - - >    ← remove the spaces between - - > to close the comment

HOW TO RUN SPECIFIC METHODS ONLY
──────────────────────────────────
    <test name="Login Tests">
        <classes>
            <class name="tests.LoginTests">
                <methods>
                    <include name="loginWithValidCredentials"/>
                    <include name="verifyLoginPageIsVisible"/>
                </methods>
            </class>
        </classes>
    </test>
-->

<suite name="AutomationExercise Test Suite" verbose="1">

